# Transport Infrastructure and Housing Affordability in London

## Overview
This project investigates housing affordability trends across London boroughs between 1997 and 2025 using Office for National Statistics (ONS) data.

The analysis explores:
- Long-term affordability deterioration
- Borough-level variation
- The relationship between Crossrail connectivity and affordability changes

## Research Question
Did transport-connected London boroughs experience stronger housing affordability deterioration between 1997 and 2025?

## Tools Used
- R
- tidyverse
- ggplot2

## Methods
- Data cleaning and transformation
- Time-series analysis
- Visualisation
- Welch Two Sample t-tests

## Key Findings
- Housing affordability worsened substantially across London boroughs between 1997–2025.
- Outer boroughs experienced some of the largest increases in unaffordability.
- Crossrail-connected boroughs did not exhibit statistically significant differences in affordability deterioration compared to non-Crossrail boroughs.

